# Copy to .env and edit. Read by scripts/container (the Apple `container`
# launcher) — NOT by the omnifeed binary, whose variables are documented in
# docs/configuration.md. .gitignore covers .env, so your values stay out of git.
#
# One KEY=value per line. `#` starts a whole-line comment only: a `#` after a
# value becomes part of the value. An exported shell variable wins over this
# file. Every line here is optional; the defaults run the stack as-is.
# See docs/apple-container.md for the full explanation of each one.

# ---- Google Programmable Search --------------------------------------------
# Your own engine id (CX). Without one, the `google cse` engine falls back to
# the id hardcoded upstream, which every SearXNG instance on the internet
# shares — Google rate-limits it globally, so the engine self-suspends on most
# queries. Create a whole-web engine at programmablesearchengine.google.com.
# It needs no API key. A private id also restores time_range filtering.
GOOGLE_CSE_CX=
# Or have any command print it (secret manager, keychain, password store):
# GOOGLE_CSE_CX_COMMAND=

# Ranking weight for that engine. Empty keeps SearXNG's default of 1.0, so it
# ranks by consensus with the rest of the pool. A result's score multiplies the
# weights of the engines that returned it, so a value above ~5 puts this
# engine's top hits above agreement between several others. Measure your own
# pool before you raise it.
GOOGLE_CSE_WEIGHT=

# ---- Brave Search API ------------------------------------------------------
# A contractual quota instead of bot detection, so it cannot be CAPTCHA-blocked.
# The free tier ended in February 2026: $5/1k requests with $5 of monthly
# credit, and SearXNG queries every enabled engine on every search. A key here
# also disables the `brave` scraper and `startpage` in the rendered settings.
BRAVEAPI_KEY=
# BRAVEAPI_KEY_COMMAND=

# ---- SearXNG settings files ------------------------------------------------
# Your own settings.yml, to change the engine pool without forking this repo.
# SEARXNG_SETTINGS=
# Where the rendered copy carrying the two credentials above is written. The
# default is searxng/settings.runtime.yml (gitignored, mode 600). Point this
# outside the repo if your policy forbids credentials in a git working tree.
# SEARXNG_RUNTIME_SETTINGS=

# ---- Names, ports, images --------------------------------------------------
# Prefix container names to run a second copy alongside this one.
# OMNIFEED_PREFIX=
# OMNIFEED_PORT_HTTP=
# OMNIFEED_PORT_MCP=
# OMNIFEED_PORT_METRICS=
# OMNIFEED_CRAWL4AI_PORT=
# OMNIFEED_CRAWL4AI_MEMORY=
# SEARXNG_IMAGE=
# CRAWL4AI_IMAGE=
# OMNIFEED_IMAGE=
